<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Install extension · <%= (settings && settings.siteName) || 'AI Note Taker' %></title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/public/auth.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/public/onboarding-web.css" />
</head>
<body class="auth-body">
  <div class="auth-shell onb-shell" style="max-width:560px">
    <a class="auth-logo" href="/">
      <span class="mark">✦</span>
      <strong><%= (settings && settings.siteName) || 'AI Note Taker' %></strong>
    </a>
    <h1>Install the Chrome extension</h1>
    <p class="auth-sub">Before the Chrome Web Store listing is live, load the extension as an unpacked package (developer mode).</p>

    <div class="auth-panel onb-panel" style="text-align:left">
      <h2 class="install-h">Option A — Load unpacked (recommended while developing)</h2>
      <ol class="install-steps">
        <li>On your machine, open the project folder and build:
          <pre>npm run build</pre>
          This creates a <code>dist/</code> folder.
        </li>
        <li>Open Chrome and go to <code>chrome://extensions</code></li>
        <li>Turn on <strong>Developer mode</strong> (top right)</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Load unpacked</strong></li>
        <li>Select the <code>dist</code> folder from the project</li>
        <li>Pin the extension, open the popup, paste your API key from <a href="/account">Account</a></li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="install-h">Option B — Share a zip with testers (still pre–Web Store)</h2>
      <ol class="install-steps">
        <li>Build: <code>npm run build</code></li>
        <li>Zip the contents of <code>dist/</code> (the files inside dist, or the folder itself)</li>
        <li>Send the zip to testers</li>
        <li>They unzip it, open <code>chrome://extensions</code> → Developer mode → <strong>Load unpacked</strong> → select the unzipped folder</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="install-h">Option C — Chrome Web Store (public release)</h2>
      <ol class="install-steps">
        <li>Create a developer account at the <a href="https://chrome.google.com/webstore/devconsole" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chrome Web Store Developer Dashboard</a></li>
        <li>Zip the <code>dist/</code> folder</li>
        <li>Upload the package, fill store listing, privacy policy, screenshots</li>
        <li>Submit for review — after approval users install with one click</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="install-note">
        <strong>Important:</strong> Put API keys only in server <code>.env</code> / user account keys — never ship long-lived provider secrets inside the public extension package.
      </div>

      <a class="auth-submit onb-install-btn" href="/account" style="margin-top:16px;display:block;text-align:center;text-decoration:none">Get my API key</a>
      <p class="auth-legal"><a href="/app">Go to my meetings</a> · <a href="/">Home</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
